  "rationale": "R-v3-1 ADD-BOTH on the HARDEST shape: the prior scope holds only the ONE missed token, so after pick 1 there is exactly one product entity left in the set - pick 1's own. The customer replies '1 and 2'; both rows are alternatives for the SAME missed token 'ax'. dymNumberedMultiSelect loops the positions through applyDymPick with slot-matching OFF. Pick 1 finds the source token by for_raw and replaces 'ax' in place with A-1. Pick 2's for_raw no longer matches (pick 1 overwrote that raw) and for_canonical is null; the for_hint fallback is SKIPPED because an earlier pick has already run on this numbered turn (issue #30) - for_hint is a SOURCE-TOKEN finder, and once the source token has been rewritten the only same-hint entity it can still find is the earlier pick's own entity, which would make ADD-BOTH last-wins. So pick 2 APPENDS, setting dym_replace_unmatched, and BOTH alternatives survive. Before the fix this fixture expected [A-2] alone (it pinned the defect); it is now the contract. The sibling ambiguous-hint fixture pins the same outcome reached by the other route, and dym-first-pick-still-uses-the-for-hint-fallback pins that the tier still fires for the FIRST pick of a turn."
